# fixedbugs, defect 2428, lane b30-shadow, 2026-11-10 (panel 243's R2).
#
# A header of the program's own, `own.h`, includes `<sys/timeb.h>`, and the
# library its group asks `pkg-config` for holds a file of that name, a name
# every platform's C library holds too. It is the library's own header, the
# one the build asked for, and the library's link comes from the same answer;
# it was refused `shadowed_header` as standing in for the C library's, so
# Homebrew's keg-only libcurl 8.23.0, whose `curl/curl.h` the SDK holds as
# well, could not be bound through a wrapper header. A folder only
# `pkg-config` names is that library's, but for a file named like one of
# C11's or POSIX.1-2024's headers. It builds and reads the library's 33.

extern "own.h" pkgconfig "p2428"
    constant TIMEB_LIB: i64

function main()
    print(TIMEB_LIB)
